{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948633-flaring-disfigurements-or-not-when-using-transmutations","id":948633,"title":"Flaring Disfigurements (or Not) When Using Transmutations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-11T08:52:36-07:00","id":948633,"title":"Flaring Disfigurements (or Not) When Using Transmutations","content":"A big deal is made about whether a Promethean reveals their Disfigurements when using their Transmutations, or if they don't and take a Condition instead; but try as I might, I can't find where in the book this system is explained. Has anyone else located it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T10:16:51-07:00","id":948666,"title":"","content":"It's in the first two paragraphs of the Transmutations section on p117.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Created body recognizes no difference between philosophy and working, and their internal alchemy becomes externally manifest. Doing so always reveals a Promethean titan\u2019s feet of clay, however, either by rending the fragile physical alchemy that hides her disfigurements, or by causing a potent supernatural Condition to dog their steps.<br /> <br /> Each Transmutation comes with an accompanying Condition, complications of the Azothic emanations of the Alembics. Charging the Alembics of a Transmutation without revealing disfigurements is <u>always</u> considered a possible source of the Condition, unless otherwise stated. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T10:27:58-07:00","id":948671,"title":"","content":"Page 171, Disfigurement paragraphs reveal that, whenever you spend pyros for <i>anything</i>, be it something innate or a Transmutation, or anything else, your human-seeming mask breaks down.<br /> <br /> That paragraph that Satchel quoted on page 117 provides an alternative to appearing as a monster in front of humans anytime you use a Transmutation in the form of the Conditions. <br /> <br /> That's pretty much it in a nut shell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T08:10:55-07:00","id":950555,"title":"","content":"Ok, but if these Conditions are caused by keeping one's Disfigurements hidden, how does one prevent their Disfigurements from appearing in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T08:12:24-07:00","id":950557,"title":"","content":"By opting to take the Condition instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T08:16:43-07:00","id":950562,"title":"","content":"Disfigurements are naturally hidden and only appear when you spend pyros for anything. Trans-Condi are exceptions to the rule - you don't have to flash your disfigurments if you take the Condition, but this is the only time you can spend pyros and not have everyone see the Disfigurements and go cray-cray. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T08:40:51-07:00","id":950572,"title":"","content":"Ok, then it should be noted in the Errata to explicitly state that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T08:46:38-07:00","id":950574,"title":"","content":"It's already explicit. Page 171 describes it. MCN just tl;dr'd it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T09:18:49-07:00","id":950587,"title":"","content":"I meant about the Conditions, not about the effect spending Pyros has on Disfigurements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T09:45:38-07:00","id":950602,"title":"","content":"Also explicit, on page 117 where it gives the overview of Transmutations - charging an Alembic always either reveals disfigurements, or causes a condition. It is also explicit in every Alembic description. I'm having trouble understanding how this could be made more clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T14:23:00-07:00","id":950746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948633-flaring-disfigurements-or-not-when-using-transmutations?p=950572#post950572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, then it should be noted in the Errata to explicitly state that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It reads pretty explicitly to me. The book is clear that you either flash your disfigurements or take the condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T18:32:07-07:00","id":950834,"title":"","content":"Yes, but it doesn't say that taking the Condition itself is what conceals the Disfigurements For all that they say, it could be an extra point of Pyros or Willpower that hides them, at the cost of taking the Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T20:33:38-07:00","id":950887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948633-flaring-disfigurements-or-not-when-using-transmutations?p=950834#post950834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but it doesn't say that taking the Condition itself is what conceals the Disfigurements</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Condition doesn't conceal the disfigurements.<br /> <br /> It <i>doesn't reveal them</i>.<br /> <br /> Your disfigurements are by-default concealed. Spending Pyros typically reveals them, but charging an Alembic can substitute the brief flare for a negative Condition associated with the Transmutation instead. It's an alternate cost to charging the Transmutation, not a side ability that does what Human Flesh does in every Alembic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T20:59:57-07:00","id":950893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948633-flaring-disfigurements-or-not-when-using-transmutations?p=950834#post950834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but it doesn't say that taking the Condition itself is what conceals the Disfigurements For all that they say, it could be an extra point of Pyros or Willpower that hides them, at the cost of taking the Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they don't say it costs an extra point of Willpower or Pyros. So it doesn't cost an extra point of Willpower or Pyros.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T09:01:35-07:00","id":951141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948633-flaring-disfigurements-or-not-when-using-transmutations?p=950887#post950887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your disfigurements are by-default concealed. Spending Pyros typically reveals them, but charging an Alembic can substitute the brief flare for a negative Condition associated with the Transmutation instead. It's an alternate cost to charging the Transmutation, not a side ability that does what Human Flesh does in every Alembic.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's all well and good, but the text never actually comes out and says that. I just think a little clarification would be helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T10:12:21-07:00","id":951181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948633-flaring-disfigurements-or-not-when-using-transmutations?p=951141#post951141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's all well and good, but the text never actually comes out and says that. I just think a little clarification would be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>It pretty much does though. I'm not sure how much more clear they can make it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:37:14-07:00","id":953588,"title":"","content":"What it says is <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>P.117 </b>- Each Transmutation comes with an accompanying Condition, complications of the Azothic emanations of the Alembics. Charging the Alembics of a Transmutation without revealing disfigurements is always considered a possible source of the Condition, unless otherwise stated. </div> </div> </div>This is essentially repeated in the description of each Transmutation, never specifically saying how the disfigurements are concealed, just stating that not revealing them when charging an Alembic imposes a Condition.<br /> To me, it reads not as &quot;a Promethean can choose to take a Condition in order to conceal her disfigurements&quot;, but rather saying that &quot;the Condition is a consequence of choosing to conceal the disfigurements&quot;, implying that some other action is needed to do the actual concealing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:51:47-07:00","id":953598,"title":"","content":"They are by default concealed. No other action is required on the Promethean's part, as his ruse is not dropped. Prometheans aren't walking around stitches out normally. Accepting the Condition is a means to keep the veneer intact despite Pyros expenditure. Pyros that should be &quot;vented&quot; instead &quot;overheats&quot; the Promethean, causing a prolonged dysfunction. Consider that there is no action described to raise the disguise, so what action could be implied?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T20:18:57-07:00","id":953615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948633-flaring-disfigurements-or-not-when-using-transmutations?p=953588#post953588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What it says is<br /> This is essentially repeated in the description of each Transmutation, never specifically saying how the disfigurements are concealed, just stating that not revealing them when charging an Alembic imposes a Condition.<br /> To me, it reads not as &quot;a Promethean can choose to take a Condition in order to conceal her disfigurements&quot;, but rather saying that &quot;the Condition is a consequence of choosing to conceal the disfigurements&quot;, implying that some other action is needed to do the actual concealing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, you're substituting &quot;[not] reveal with &quot;conceal&quot; despite these things not being interchangeable. The bit on p.171 is fairly clear that a Promethean's disfigurements are normally concealed to unCreated eyes in the absence of Pyros expenditure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T17:08:09-07:00","id":954111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948633-flaring-disfigurements-or-not-when-using-transmutations?p=953615#post953615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, you're substituting &quot;[not] reveal with &quot;conceal&quot; despite these things not being interchangeable. The bit on p.171 is fairly clear that a Promethean's disfigurements are normally concealed to unCreated eyes in the absence of Pyros expenditure.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, but for example <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>P.134</b> - Charging a Disquietism Distillation without flaring disfigurements imposes the Irritable Condition </div> </div> </div>To me, this says exactly two things: <br /> 1. There are two ways to charge Distillations, one that flares disfigurements and one that doesn't; and <br /> 2. The method that doesn't flare disfigurements imposes a Transmutation's negative Condition.<br /> <br /> At no point in the book does it explicitly say that taking the Condition in and of itself is the action that prevents the disfigurements from flaring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T17:36:49-07:00","id":954120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948633-flaring-disfigurements-or-not-when-using-transmutations?p=954111#post954111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, but for example <br /> To me, this says exactly two things: <br /> 1. There are two ways to charge Distillations, one that flares disfigurements and one that doesn't; and <br /> 2. The method that doesn't flare disfigurements imposes a Transmutation's negative Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>These things are both correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948633-flaring-disfigurements-or-not-when-using-transmutations?p=954111#post954111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At no point in the book does it explicitly say that taking the Condition in and of itself is the action that prevents the disfigurements from flaring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking the Condition isn't the thing that prevents the Disfigurements from flaring. The Condition is a consequence of the method that doesn't cause Disfigurements to flare. And since the method that doesn't cost Disfigurements to flare doesn't have any additional cost listed, it doesn't have one.<br /> <br /> I'm really not seeing any part of this that would cause this much confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T17:38:53-07:00","id":954123,"title":"","content":"Let me try phrasing it a different way. When you charge a Distillation, flaring your Disfigurements is optional. But, if you opt not to flare your Disfigurements, you get a Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T18:13:44-07:00","id":954135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>The Created body recognizes no difference between philosophy and working, and their internal alchemy becomes externally manifest. Doing so always reveals a Promethean titan\u2019s feet of clay, however,<b> either</b> by rending the fragile physical alchemy that hides her disfigurements, <b>or</b> by causing a potent supernatural Condition to dog their steps.</i> </div> </div> </div>Taking the Condition is explicitly the thing that prevents the Disfigurement from flaring. You are substituting one for the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T08:29:28-07:00","id":954399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948633-flaring-disfigurements-or-not-when-using-transmutations?p=954111#post954111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, but for example <br /> To me, this says exactly two things: <br /> 1. There are two ways to charge Distillations, one that flares disfigurements and one that doesn't; and <br /> 2. The method that doesn't flare disfigurements imposes a Transmutation's negative Condition.<br /> <br /> At no point in the book does it explicitly say that taking the Condition in and of itself is the action that prevents the disfigurements from flaring.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Promethean doesn't think, &quot;I'm going to become Irritable to hide my disfigurements.&quot; The Promethean thinks, &quot;I can't let them see my disfigurements.&quot; The Promethean manages to prevent the glimpse of his true form, but the act of doing so makes him Irritable. It's cause and effect. Taking the Condition doesn't cause the disfigurements to remain hidden. Keeping the disfigurements hidden causes the Condition. The player of the character may decide to take a Condition to keep the character's disfigurements hidden, but the character just decides not to reveal them. Without having the book handy, I can't be certain, but I'd guess that at least some characters might not even make the connection between the Condition and the efforts to not reveal their disfigurements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T19:47:54-07:00","id":955367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948633-flaring-disfigurements-or-not-when-using-transmutations?p=954123#post954123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me try phrasing it a different way. When you charge a Distillation, flaring your Disfigurements is optional. But, if you opt not to flare your Disfigurements, you get a Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, now <i>that</i> makes sense to me. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T20:29:23-07:00","id":955384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/948633-flaring-disfigurements-or-not-when-using-transmutations?p=955367#post955367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, now <i>that</i> makes sense to me. Thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}